Floor derivation: NOT APPLIED, kept as the starting point for the sampling fix
==============================================================================

This patch adds the runtime derivation of SQUEEZE_FLOOR described in HANDOFF 10.6.
It was written, built and run on device on 2026-09-11, and it is deliberately NOT
in the tree.

Why it is not applied: the algebra is right but the sampling point is wrong.

    floor = knee + containerTy()          where knee = C - maxSpace
    C     = notifPre + y                  a build constant (2294 on this device)

That reproduces the hardcoded 740 exactly - but only in the NORMAL keyguard layout,
where maxSpace reads 1386. Cover mode puts the keyguard into its notification layout,
where maxSpace reads 1196, and there the same formula yields 7.7. learnFloorY() is
called at the top of enterCoverMode(), by which point the layout has already swapped,
so on every real entry its own sanity guard rejected the result and kept 740:

    floor: derived 200.6 (C 2294.0 knee 1098.0 refT -897.4) out of range, keeping 740.0

The mechanism is sound and the fields are real; only the moment of sampling is wrong.
The fix is to sample from the setNotifY hook while sHoldY == null, not at entry - that
is the only place the normal layout is observable with a known natural y.

Applying this patch as-is will build and run, and will change nothing on this device:
every derivation is rejected by the range guard. It is here so the next attempt starts
from working code rather than from the algebra again.

Apply with:  git apply docs/floor-derivation-not-applied.patch
